  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: Welcome to Neptune the distant blue giant at the edge of the solar system,
    ruled by extreme winds and deep cold. Neptune is an ice giant similar to Uranus,
    made mostly of water, ammonia, and methane, which gives it its vivid blue color.
    Despite being so far from the Sun, Neptune is incredibly active, with the fastest
    winds ever recorded on any planet, reaching speeds faster than sound. Massive
    dark storms churn through its atmosphere, appearing and disappearing over time.
    Neptune has faint rings and a collection of moons, including Triton, which orbits
    backward and is geologically active with icy geysers. Dark, powerful, and unpredictable,
    Neptune is a dramatic and dangerous world.
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
