  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Welcome to Venus a mysterious and hostile world often called Earth\u2019s
    twin, but far from friendly. Venus is the second planet from the Sun and is nearly
    the same size as Earth, yet its surface is one of the most extreme environments
    in the solar system. Thick clouds of sulfuric acid blanket the planet, trapping
    heat in a runaway greenhouse effect that makes Venus the hottest planet, with
    surface temperatures hot enough to melt lead. Its atmosphere is dense and toxic,
    composed mostly of carbon dioxide, creating crushing pressure far greater than
    Earth\u2019s. Volcanoes, vast lava plains, and deformed mountains cover its surface,
    hinting at a violent geological past that may still be active today. Venus rotates
    very slowly and in the opposite direction of most planets, meaning a single day
    on Venus is longer than its entire year. Shrouded in clouds and extreme conditions,
    Venus is a dangerous but fascinating planet."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
