  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Ice is one of the most abundant and defining resources found on Neptune,
    dominating the planet\u2019s structure and environment. Unlike ordinary ice,
    Neptune\u2019s ice is made up of frozen water, ammonia, and methane, existing
    under immense pressure and extreme cold. These icy materials form thick layers
    beneath the atmosphere and are constantly shaped by powerful storms and internal
    heat. On Neptune\u2019s moons and in its upper layers, ice appears as deep blue
    and white formations, hardened by temperatures far below anything experienced
    on Earth. Once harvested and processed, ice is essential for life support, fuel
    production, cooling systems, and advanced chemical synthesis."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
