  m_text: Welcome to Mars the red planet, a cold and dusty world that has fascinated
    explorers for generations. Mars is the fourth planet from the Sun and is known
    for its rusty red surface, caused by iron oxide spread across its soil and rocks.
    It has a thin atmosphere made mostly of carbon dioxide, which offers little protection
    from radiation and keeps the planet cold. Mars is home to some of the most extreme
    landmarks in the solar system, including Olympus Mons, the tallest volcano ever
    discovered, and Valles Marineris, a canyon system that dwarfs anything on Earth.
    Evidence suggests Mars once had flowing rivers, lakes, and possibly oceans, raising
    the possibility that life may have existed there long ago. Today, Mars experiences
    massive dust storms, frozen polar ice caps, and long seasons.
