      m_Calls: []
  m_text: Gold ore is one of the most sought-after and precious resources found on
    Earth, prized for its beauty, rarity, and unique properties. It appears naturally
    as bright yellow metallic veins or tiny flakes embedded in rock, often found
    in quartz and ancient river deposits. Gold is far less common than iron and forms
    through intense geological processes deep within the Earth, making its deposits
    harder to locate and mine. Despite being soft in its natural state, gold is incredibly
    valuable it does not rust, corrode, or degrade over time, and it conducts electricity
    extremely well. Once refined, gold is used to craft jewelry, currency, and advanced
    electronics.
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
