      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Welcome to Saturn the jewel of the solar system, famous for its breathtaking
    rings and immense beauty. Saturn is a massive gas giant made mostly of hydrogen
    and helium, similar to Jupiter, but slightly smaller and far less dense. Its
    iconic rings are made of countless pieces of ice, rock, and dust, ranging from
    tiny grains to mountain-sized chunks, all orbiting in perfect harmony. Saturn\u2019s
    atmosphere is filled with powerful winds and storms, including a strange hexagon-shaped
    weather pattern at its north pole. Like other gas giants, Saturn has no solid
    surface, with pressure increasing dramatically the deeper you go. The planet
    is surrounded by many fascinating moons, including Titan, which has lakes of
    liquid methane, and Enceladus, which sprays icy plumes into space. Elegant yet
    extreme, Saturn is an incredible planet."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
