      m_Calls: []
  m_text: Welcome to Mercury the smallest and fastest planet in the solar system,
    racing closest around the Sun. Mercury is a rocky, crater-covered world with
    almost no atmosphere, leaving its surface exposed to space and extreme temperature
    swings. During the day, temperatures soar hot enough to melt metal, while at
    night they plunge to freezing cold, creating one of the harshest environments
    imaginable. With no thick air to protect it, Mercury is constantly scarred by
    meteor impacts, giving it a surface similar to the Moon. Despite being so close
    to the Sun, some craters near its poles hide permanent ice, trapped in eternal
    shadow. A year on Mercury lasts only 88 Earth days, but its slow rotation means
    one day feels incredibly long. Silent, scorched, and ancient, Mercury is a stark
    and unforgiving planet.
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
