      m_Calls: []
  m_text: Welcome to Uranus the most unusual planet in the solar system, known for
    its extreme tilt and icy nature. Uranus is an ice giant made mostly of water,
    ammonia, and methane, giving it a cold blue-green color. Unlike other planets,
    Uranus is tilted on its side, causing it to roll around the Sun and experience
    the most extreme seasons, where each pole can face sunlight or darkness for decades
    at a time. Its atmosphere is one of the coldest in the solar system, with fierce
    winds and a calm-looking but deceptive appearance. Uranus has faint rings and
    many moons, all orbiting around its tilted axis in a bizarre and alien arrangement.
    Strange, frozen, and silent, Uranus is a perfect planet.
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
